<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Danish–Icelandic Act of Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Danish–Icelandic Act of Union was an agreement between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and Iceland that took effect on 1 December 1918, recognising Iceland as a fully sovereign kingdom in personal union with Denmark under King Christian X. Denmark handled Iceland's foreign affairs on its behalf, and either side could end the union after 25 years. Iceland did so and became a republic in 1944.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/danish-icelandic-act-of-union.jpg" alt="Danish–Icelandic Act of Union" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willem Blaeu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1630_IJsland_Blaeu_HR%27.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
